export anchor VideoTimelineStyle:
    number: 313
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Video timeline
    idea: A video editor where services sit in a bin as clips, a program monitor shows the frame at the 07.48 playhead, an inspector holds the incident, and a multi track timeline lays out the 24 hours as video and audio tracks with markers.
    base: dark
    palette:
        suite: #16151c, the page
        pane: #211f29, panes
        paneHead: #2a2834, pane titles, track headers and the ruler
        well: #0f0e14, track wells, bin tiles and fields
        rule: #3a3746, borders and rules
        ink: #ecebf3, text
        muted: #aba7bd, labels and timecodes
        video: #5865d8, video clips, the requests filmstrip, the primary button and the focus halo
        audio: #2e8a5a, audio clips under #7ff0b0 waveforms
        playhead: #ff5c7a, the playhead, the timecode readout and the current app underline
        amber: #ffbe55, the incident clip, Degraded and Investigating
        green: #74e0a0, Healthy and Resolved
        sky: #86c8ff, Recovered
        rose: #ff7f8f, the error trace and Firing
    type:
        Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at 13px and
        1.45, with ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas for timecode,
        service names and track tags. The monitor title card is up to 30px
        bold, the incident number 20px mono bold amber, the timecode
        readout 18px mono in the playhead colour, track tags 11px mono bold.
    layout:
        A black bar holds Brightwork Ops, the apps as workspace links with
        a playhead coloured underline on Ops, and Sequence Production last
        24 hours. Three panes follow. The bin shows the services as clip
        tiles, each a 16 by 9 thumbnail with a large status shape and the
        uptime as a duration badge, then the name, word and metric. The
        program monitor shows the frame at the playhead, safe area guides,
        a timecode overlay and a title card reading billing 5xx rate above
        2 percent with the error spike, then playback buttons and a note
        that billing recovered six minutes later. The inspector holds the
        incident as property rows. The full width timeline has a markers
        row with alert flags, a timecode ruler, V3 Incident as an amber
        clip from 06.58, V2 Deploys as three staggered clips, V1 Requests
        as a filmstrip of 24 frames with bar heights, and A1 to A3 as audio
        waveforms for error rate, p95 and p50, with a playhead line at
        07.48. Markers and an edit list close the screen. The monitor moves
        first below 1100px and the timeline scrolls inside itself on phones.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 8px gutters between panes, 6 to 10px pane padding, 44px per hour.
    density: Dense. Three panes over an eight row timeline.
    corners: 4px panes, tiles and buttons, 3px clips and markers.
    borders: 1px #3a3746, clips carry a lighter border of their colour, a dashed safe area in the monitor.
    shadows: None. Wells sit darker than panes.
    icons:
        Large status shapes as bin thumbnails and 14px shapes on markers,
        chips and lists, a ringed tick for Healthy, a triangle for
        Degraded, a circular arrow for Recovered, a bolt for Firing, a tick
        for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
    focus: A 2px white outline offset 2px with a video blue halo.
    tone: Editing words, such as Bin, Program, Inspector, In point, Markers and Edit list.
